// An `@attribute` struct may give a field a default (`ttl: int = 60`), object-model slice 6i. Such a
// field is **optional** in a `#[...]` construction — `#[Cache]` omits both, `#[Cache(ttl: 5)]` omits
// only `eager` — and materialization fills each omitted field from its declared default, so
// `attributes_of` reports the default, not a placeholder. Both backends fill the same defaults, so
// the differential agrees.
// expect: stdout "60 false"
// expect: stdout "5 true"
// expect: exit 0
@attribute
struct Cache { ttl: int = 60  eager: bool = false }

#[Cache]
struct A { id: int }

#[Cache(ttl: 5, eager: true)]
struct B { id: int }

for c in attributes_of::<Cache>() {
    echo "${c.value.ttl} ${c.value.eager}"
}
